	A good password includes a mixture of letters, numbers, and symbolic
	characters and is longer than six characters.  One way to build good,
	memorable passwords is to combine nonsense syllables like ang, fof, or
	lal.  A password such as ANG..FOF is difficult for someone to guess.

	For example, suppose Alexis has an initial password DEFENDER, which
	the system manager assigned.  After learning to log on and off the
	system, Alexis chooses a truly private password such as SAN..TOR.
	To change DEFENDER to SAN..TOR, Alexis does the following:

	Alexis starts logging on by pressing the New Line key:

	... Press NEW LINE to begin logging on ...

	<NL>

	AOS/VS displays its banner and prompts for username and password.
	Alexis types the usual username/password combination of Alexis and
	DEFENDER.  However, instead of pressing the New Line key after
	DEFENDER, Alexis presses the Erase Page key:

	... EXEC n date ...
	Username:  Alexis <NL>
	Password:  defender (which doesn't echo) <Erase Page>

	And AOS/VS prompts for the new password, which Alexis types

    |   Enter your new password:   san..tor (which doesn't echo) <NL>
    |
    |   To help keep the password secure and secret, the system will not echo
    |   (display) any keystrokes Alexis enters in response to the "Enter your
    |   new password" prompt.  Instead of showing what Alexis typed, the system
    |   asks Alexis to confirm the new password by password by typing it again:
    |
    |           Reenter new password for validation:
    |
    |   Alexis types SAN..TOR after the "Reenter..." prompt, again without
    |   seeing the entry displayed on the terminal.
    |
    |   If you make a mistake while typing the password a second time, AOS/VS
    |   will display a "does not match" message; then it will ask for the new
    |   password and validation again.  AOS/VS will let you try five times to
    |   specify and validate a new password.  If it does not receive a valid
    |   pair in five tries, it informs you that the old password will remain
    |   in effect with the following message:
    |
    |           --Password not changed--


