	Summary

	In this section you prepared a terminal for the upcoming session
	with AOS/VS; you noted the features of your computer keyboard and
	became familiar with username/password pairs.  You now know how to
	log on and off the sytem, and how to change your password.  You also
	have some idea of how to maintain the privacy of your account.


				Getting Your Bearings

	As mentioned earlier, the CLI is the command language (or interactive
	monitor) for AOS/VS.  You use its commands to gain access to all the
	programs and services available under AOS/VS.  Some CLI commands,
	such as the ones we look at in this section, orient you to AOS/VS.
	They provide you with such general information as the time of day,
	the date, and your location within the system.


