	The Permanence attribute, if on, prevents any directory or
	non-directory file from being deleted by any user.
    |   With AOS/VS, a file's permanence does not affect its parent
    |   directory; you can delete a directory whose files have permanence
    |   set.  AOS/VS II, on the other hand, will not not let you delete a
    |   directory if a file anywhere within it has permanence set on.
